  </div>

  <div class="main-grid">
  <article class="panel chart-panel">
    <div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">MARKET DATA · DERIV MT5</p><h2 id="chartTitle">Volatility index</h2></div><div class="control-group"><select id="symbolSelect" aria-label="Select broker symbol"></select><select id="timeframeSelect" aria-label="Select timeframe"><option>M1</option><option selected>M5</option><option>M15</option><option>H1</option><option>H4</option><option>D1</option></select></div></div>
    <div class="chart-meta"><span id="lastPrice" class="quote">—</span><span id="priceChange" class="price-diff">—</span><span class="mini-source">Completed broker candles</span></div>
    <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="marketChart" role="img" aria-label="Historical Deriv broker candlestick chart"></canvas><div class="chart-empty" id="chartEmpty">Loading broker candles…</div></div>
    <div class="chart-footer"><span>Broker source: Deriv MT5 DEMO</span><span id="chartUpdated">Last refresh: —</span></div>
  </article>
  <article class="panel decision-panel">
    <div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">ORIGINAL TRADINGAGENTS + LOCAL QWEN</p><h2>Latest AI decision</h2></div><span class="chip" id="agentCycleChip">CHECKING</span></div>
    <p class="last-symbol" id="decisionSymbol">Waiting for decision</p>
    <div class="decision-card"><div><span>Technical direction</span><strong id="technicalAction">—</strong></div><div class="separator">→</div><div><span>Agent rating</span><strong id="agentRating">—</strong></div></div>
    <div class="final-decision"><span>FINAL SHADOW DIRECTION</span><strong id="shadowAction">—</strong></div>
    <p class="decision-reason" id="decisionReason">The first verified decision will appear here.</p>
    <div class="decision-bottom"><div><span>AI model</span><b id="decisionModel">—</b></div><div><span>Recorded at</span><b id="decisionTime">—</b></div></div>
  </article>
  </div>

  <div class="bottom-grid">
    <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">AUTOMATIC RESEARCH</p><h2>Decision history</h2></div><button class="textbutton" data-jump="signals">All decisions ›</button></div><div id="signalPreview" class="history-rows"><div class="empty">Loading decision journal…</div></div></article>
    <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">INFRASTRUCTURE</p><h2>System health</h2></div><button class="textbutton" data-jump="systems">Details ›</button></div><div id="servicePreview" class="service-list"><div class="empty">Checking system services…</div></div></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="compare" class="view">
  <article class="panel" style="margin-bottom:18px">
    <div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">DERIV DEMO MT5 · 8 VERIFIED TIMEFRAMES</p><h2>APEX strategy signal vs. completed candle and EMA/RSI trend</h2></div><select id="comparisonSymbol" aria-label="Select instrument for candle comparison"></select></div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top:-4px">APEX uses only the connected <b>Deriv USD DEMO MT5</b> terminal. Single-candle direction compares the last completed candle's close with its open; EMA/RSI trend uses multiple completed broker candles. Neither display sends orders or depends on another trading platform.</p>
    <div class="account-strip comparison-strip">
      <article class="metric comparison-decision"><span>APEX STRATEGY SIGNAL · SAME AS SCANNER</span><strong id="comparisonStrategyGate">VERIFYING</strong><small id="comparisonStrategyGateMeta">Only displays a decision when the scanner uses the identical broker snapshot</small></article>
      <article class="metric"><span>M5 CANDLE BODY · NOT A TRADE SIGNAL</span><strong id="comparisonM5Bias">—</strong><small id="comparisonM5Time">Waiting for candle timestamp</small></article>
      <article class="metric"><span>M5 MULTI-CANDLE EMA/RSI TREND</span><strong id="comparisonM5Trend">—</strong><small id="comparisonM5Direction">M5 strategy direction pending</small></article>
      <article class="metric"><span>SCANNER / BROKER SNAPSHOT SYNC</span><strong id="comparisonSource">—</strong><small id="comparisonFreshness">Checking independent MT5 source</small></article>
    </div>
    <div class="notice"><span class="notice-icon">◈</span><div><b id="comparisonScannerMatch">Verifying Strategy Scanner alignment</b><span id="comparisonScannerDetails">Checking M5 candle timestamp, indicators and final strategy gate against the scanner.</span><span id="comparisonScannerReason">Waiting for current broker candle evidence.</span></div></div>
    <p class="muted"><b>Only APEX Strategy Signal is the trading-strategy decision.</b> The M5 candle body (close minus open) is descriptive price movement, not a BUY/SELL recommendation. Scanner entry also requires M15/H1/H4 trend agreement and RSI confirmation; Crash/Boom need a tested spike model. Identical broker candle timestamps are required to compare these pages. This panel does not submit orders.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Timeframe</th><th>Candle body (NOT a signal)</th><th>EMA/RSI trend</th><th>Open</th><th>Close</th><th>Closed at (UTC)</th><th>Time since close</th></tr></thead><tbody id="comparisonRows"><tr><td colspan="7">Loading verified broker candles…</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="table-foot">All timestamps are actual candle closing times, not opening times. M3/M30 EMA/RSI trend is marked unavailable because the supplemental feed currently provides only completed-candle observations, not enough bars for an EMA21 history. No execution signal is implied.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section id="account" class="view">
  <div class="kpis">
    <article class="metric"><span>Balance · USD</span><strong id="accountBalance">—</strong><small>Broker-confirmed DEMO</small></article>
    <article class="metric"><span>Equity · USD</span><strong id="accountEquity">—</strong><small>Current account snapshot</small></article>
    <article class="metric"><span>Free margin · USD</span><strong id="accountFreeMargin">—</strong><small>Not available for automatic execution</small></article>
    <article class="metric"><span>Today's realized P&amp;L · USD</span><strong id="accountTodayPnl">—</strong><small>All broker trades, not APEX-only</small></article>
  </div>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">OFFICIAL DERIV MT5 ACCOUNT</p><h2>Open positions</h2></div><span class="chip" id="accountFreshness">CHECKING</span></div>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Ticket</th><th>Opened at · UTC</th><th>Symbol</th><th>Side</th><th>Volume</th><th>Open</th><th>Current</th><th>Stop</th><th>Target</th><th>Floating USD</th></tr></thead><tbody id="accountPositions"></tbody></table></div>
  <p class="table-foot">Position opening date/time comes from the MT5 broker position record (UTC). No order-entry controls are enabled.</p></article>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">OFFICIAL BROKER HISTORY</p><h2>Recent execution deals</h2></div><span class="chip">HISTORICAL / ALL SOURCES</span></div>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Executed at · UTC</th><th>Deal ID</th><th>Symbol</th><th>Side</th><th>Event</th><th>Volume</th><th>Price</th><th>Gross P&amp;L</th><th>Net cashflow</th></tr></thead><tbody id="accountDeals"></tbody></table></div>
  <p class="table-foot">Every deal is stamped using the MT5 broker execution time (UTC), including entry and exit deals. Historical broker trades were not necessarily created by APEX.</p></article>
</section>

<section id="scanner" class="view">
  <div class="kpis">
    <article class="metric"><span>Instruments scanned</span><strong id="scanSymbols">—</strong><small>Volatility, Crash &amp; Boom</small></article>
    <article class="metric"><span>Research proposals</span><strong id="scanCandidates">—</strong><small>Not actionable without certification</small></article>
    <article class="metric"><span>Scanner freshness</span><strong id="scanFreshness">—</strong><small id="scanAge">Checking scanner output</small></article>
    <article class="metric"><span>Research governor (legacy)</span><strong id="scanRisk">LOCKED</strong><small>Separate from controlled DEMO v2</small></article>
  </div>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">DETERMINISTIC MULTI-TIMEFRAME RESEARCH</p><h2>All 13 Deriv strategy proposals</h2></div><button class="textbutton" data-jump="compare">Compare closed candles ›</button></div>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Instrument</th><th>Family</th><th>M1 trend</th><th>M5 candle body (NOT signal)</th><th>M5 EMA/RSI trend</th><th>M5 EMA/RSI direction</th><th>M15 trend</th><th>H1 trend</th><th>H4 trend</th><th>D1 trend</th><th>RSI M5</th><th>APEX Strategy Signal</th><th>Legacy research lock</th><th>$140 DEMO status</th><th>Evidence / Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody id="scannerBody"></tbody></table></div>
  <p class="table-foot">**M5 candle** = direction of one completed candle (same method as V7). **M5 EMA trend** = multi-candle EMA/RSI direction. **Strategy Gate** = additional entry rules. These are three different calculations, not interchangeable BUY/SELL signals. UP means EMA9 &gt; EMA21 with confirming RSI; DOWN means EMA9 &lt; EMA21 with confirming RSI. Experimental EMA/RSI logic using completed Deriv candles. Crash/Boom research is held pending dedicated spike-model testing. Legacy research lock is not the same as the separately verified $140 DEMO controller. The DEMO status column shows broker-confirmed positions when available, or states why an entry is waiting. A strategy proposal is not a guaranteed profitable or executed trade.</p></article>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">ACCOUNT-WIDE DEMO RISK</p><h2>Independent Risk Governor</h2></div><span class="chip">FAIL CLOSED</span></div>
  <div class="risk-numbers"><div><span>Daily loss headroom · USD</span><strong id="governorHeadroom">—</strong></div><div><span>Per-order risk allowance · USD</span><strong id="governorSingle">—</strong></div><div><span>Kill switch</span><strong id="governorKill">LOCKED</strong></div></div>
  <p class="muted" id="governorNotes">The risk governor independently validates broker snapshots, active positions, aggregate exposure, loss history and minimum-lot USD estimates.</p>
  <p class="warning-copy">Legacy research governor remains locked; controlled DEMO execution uses its own independently checked $140 USD account-loss admission budget. LIVE stays disabled. Broker stops may slip beyond estimated loss.</p></article>
</section>

<section id="execution" class="view">
  <div class="kpis">
    <article class="metric"><span>Broker directions tested</span><strong id="execEvaluated">—</strong><small>13 instruments × BUY and SELL</small></article>
    <article class="metric"><span>MT5 checks accepted</span><strong id="execAccepted">—</strong><small>Official order_check, not actual fills</small></article>
    <article class="metric"><span>Broker-confirmed APEX orders</span><strong id="execOrders">0</strong><small id="execOrdersNote">Never count prechecks as fills</small></article>
    <article class="metric"><span>Controlled DEMO controller</span><strong id="execLock">CHECKING</strong><small id="execGateNote">Verified status from APEX DEMO v2</small></article>
  </div>
  <div class="notice"><span class="notice-icon">◈</span><div><b>Prechecks do not place trades</b><span>The legacy broker precheck table tests minimum-lot ATR requests. The new USD workbook profile above is independently validated in the controlled DEMO execution engine; prechecks are not broker fills.</span></div></div>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">BROKER-NATIVE CONTROLLED DEMO · LIVE EXECUTION STATE</p><h2>Automatic M5 DEMO orders · $140 account cap</h2></div><span class="chip" id="demoCycleFreshness">CHECKING</span></div>
    <div class="risk-numbers">
      <div><span>Daily remaining budget · USD</span><strong id="demoBudgetRemaining">—</strong></div>
      <div><span>Confirmed APEX positions opened</span><strong id="demoConfirmedTotal">0</strong></div>
      <div><span>Unreconciled attempts</span><strong id="demoUncertainTotal">0</strong></div>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" id="demoLastReason">Awaiting the next controlled DEMO cycle.</p>
    <p class="table-foot">This controller is separate from the legacy research intent preview. A qualified M5 signal is required. The USD cap uses broker cashflows and modelled stop exposure, not a guaranteed maximum fill loss.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div>
    <p class="panel-kicker">DERIV INDICES.XLSX · USER CONFIGURATION + LOT OVERRIDES</p>
    <h2>Active USD lot / stop-loss / take-profit profile · 13 symbols (Excel + overrides)</h2>
  </div><span class="chip" id="demoProfileState">VERIFYING</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Instrument</th><th>Configured lot</th><th>Stop-loss · USD</th><th>Take-profit · USD</th><th>Budget admission</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="demoUsdProfiles"><tr><td colspan="5">Verifying broker-backed USD profile</td></tr></tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p class="table-foot">USD amounts represent broker-calculated gross position P&amp;L, not MT5 points. Commission, fees, spread, swap and slippage can alter net realized P&amp;L. $100 stops require a ~$130 buffered risk allowance and are checked against the remaining $140 account-loss admission budget; quoted stop-loss and realized net loss can differ. A qualified M5 strategy signal and broker precheck are required separately.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">OFFICIAL DERIV USD DEMO · BROKER ORDER VALIDATION</p><h2>Broker-native stop/target prechecks</h2></div><span class="chip" id="execFreshness">CHECKING</span></div>
    <div class="execution-market-strip" role="group" aria-label="UTC market clock and broker precheck freshness">
      <div><span>Market time · UTC</span><strong id="executionMarketTimeUtc">--:--:-- UTC</strong></div>
      <div><span>Market date · UTC</span><strong id="executionMarketDateUtc">-- --- ----</strong></div>
      <div><span>Last MT5 check</span><strong id="executionCheckAge">CHECKING</strong></div>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Instrument</th><th>Side</th><th>Minimum lot</th><th>Stop-loss</th><th>Take-profit</th><th>Buffered loss · USD</th><th>Broker check</th><th>Checked at · UTC</th></tr></thead><tbody id="execPrechecks"></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="table-foot">Each check timestamp comes from the MT5 precheck collector. Older checks show their batch snapshot time until individual check timestamps are available. These are validations, not trades or fills. Risk estimates are not guaranteed loss limits.</p></article>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">DURABLE SQLITE EXECUTION INTENT JOURNAL</p><h2>Duplicate prevention and recovery state</h2></div><span class="chip">LEGACY RESEARCH PREVIEW</span></div>
    <div class="risk-numbers"><div><span>Unique signal intents</span><strong id="execIntents">—</strong></div><div><span>Unreconciled orders</span><strong id="execUncertain">—</strong></div><div><span>Execution state</span><strong id="execMode">LOCKED</strong></div></div>
    <p class="muted">Signal identities survive service restarts. Unexpected/uncertain states prevent attempts from being repeated automatically.</p></article>
</section>

<section id="markets" class="view">
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">BROKER DATA / 13 SYNTHETIC INSTRUMENTS</p><h2>Market watch</h2></div><input id="marketSearch" class="search" type="search" placeholder="Search instruments…" aria-label="Search instruments"></div>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Instrument</th><th>Last close</th><th>M5 change</th><th>M15</th><th>H1</th><th>H4</th><th>Last candle (UTC)</th></tr></thead><tbody id="marketsBody"></tbody></table></div>
  <p class="table-foot">Values use the last completed broker candles. Trend = 9/21-period EMA comparison, not trade authorization.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section id="signals" class="view">
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">PERSISTENT DECISION JOURNAL</p><h2>TradingAgents decisions</h2></div><span class="chip">SHADOW MODE</span></div>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Recorded (UTC)</th><th>Symbol</th><th>Technical</th><th>AI rating</th><th>Final shadow</th><th>Execution</th></tr></thead><tbody id="signalsBody"></tbody></table></div>
  <p class="table-foot">A BUY or SELL research direction does not execute an order. Order execution requires separately verified risk controls and authorization.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section id="systems" class="view">
  <div class="system-grid">
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">SERVICE SUPERVISION</p><h2>Infrastructure services</h2></div></div><div id="serviceDetails" class="service-list"></div></article>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">CONTRACT-LOSS ESTIMATES · DEMO</p><h2>Broker contract risk</h2></div></div>
    <div class="risk-numbers"><div><span>Verified contract estimates</span><strong id="riskBelow">—</strong></div><div><span>Unverified contracts</span><strong id="riskAbove">—</strong></div></div>
    <p class="muted" id="riskAge">Risk assessment not yet loaded.</p><p class="warning-copy">These are hypothetical single-trade estimates from MT5 contract calculations. They are <b>not</b> an enforceable cumulative-loss limit, trade authorization or a guarantee against slippage.</p>
  </article>
  </div>
  <article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><p class="panel-kicker">DERIV CONTRACT SPECIFICATIONS</p><h2>Minimum-lot estimated stop losses</h2></div></div>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Instrument</th><th>Minimum lot</th><th>BUY estimated loss</th><th>SELL estimated loss</th><th>Validation</th></tr></thead><tbody id="riskBody"></tbody></table></div></article>
</section>
</main>
